 "title": "Played Acid Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: the acid squelch under your own fingers: a screaming resonant filter on every note, sliding when you play legato.\n\nHow it's built: a saw, its pitch through a Slew (legato notes slide), into the Ladder filter with RESONANCE very high; a short envelope squelches the CUTOFF on each note; Drive after for grit; a short Delay. One voice.\n\nPlay: fast sixteenth-note bass parts; overlap notes for slides; play the filter's CUTOFF with your other hand (LEARN it to a knob).\n\nTweak: CUTOFF, RESONANCE, the filter's CV, the envelope's DECAY, DRIVE.",
